    "report": "The fix is committed, but on a new branch rather than `main`, which was the branch checked out when I started. I did that because the repo guidance says to branch first when on the default branch. `main` is untouched, so the commit can be moved there if you want it.\n\n**Why the contact details came back**\n\nThe conversation view decides whether to show contact details in full by asking Booking `hasPaidStay(travellerId, listingId)`. That query, in `src/Contexts/Booking/Infrastructure/PostgresBookingQueries.ts`, had an extra condition, `AND b.status <> 'cancelled'`. Once the booking was cancelled, the query found no paid stay, so the details were masked again.\n\nPayment status is not changed by a cancellation. Refunds only move the refund status, so the payment stays `paid` or `declared`. That means the booking-status condition was the only thing hiding the details.\n\n**The fix**\n\n- Removed `AND b.status <> 'cancelled'` from `hasPaidStay`. The query now answers only whether a traveller's booking for the listing has a payment that is `paid` or `declared`, which matches the port's documented contract (\"whatever the booking's status now\").\n- Extended the existing e2e test `hides them from the reader but the sender until a stay is paid, then shows everything in full` in `conversations.routes.e2e.spec.ts`. After the traveller cancels the paid booking, the host's phone-number-style message must still be shown in full to the traveller.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- The full e2e suite ran: 114 suites, 607 tests, all passing. My `--testPathPatterns` filter was ignored, so this was the whole suite, not just the conversations file.\n- `yarn typecheck`, `eslint` and `prettier --check` pass on the two changed files.\n- I did not revert the fix to confirm the new assertion fails without it. The logic makes that clear, but I have not observed it.\n\n**What was unclear**\n\n- The task said \"the current branch\" and the current branch was `main`. I chose a new branch, `fix/contact-details-after-cancel`, per the repo's default-branch rule.\n- I did not push.\n\nCommit: `ac35c7d` on `fix/contact-details-after-cancel`.",
